{"id":"mahabharata-7-073","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":73,"title":"त्रिसप्ततितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 73 · Drona against Satyaki","summary":{"en":"Satyaki rescues Dhrishtadyumna, and Drona, seeing his marvellous feat, fights him with arrows that darken the field. The armies are covered in dust and cannot be distinguished.","kn":"ಸಾತ್ಯಕಿ ಧೃಷ್ಟದ್ಯುಮ್ನನನ್ನು ರಕ್ಷಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅವನ ಅದ್ಭುತ ಸಾಹಸ ಕಂಡ ದ್ರೋಣ ರಣರಂಗ ಕಪ್ಪಾಗಿಸುವ ಬಾಣಗಳಿಂದ ಅವನೊಡನೆ ಹೋರಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಸೈನ್ಯಗಳು ಧೂಳಿನಿಂದ ಮುಚ್ಚಿ ಗುರುತಿಸಲಾಗುವುದಿಲ್ಲ.","hi":"सात्यकि धृष्टद्युम्न को बचाता है, और उसका अद्भुत कर्म देखकर द्रोण रणभूमि को अँधेरा करने वाले बाणों से उससे लड़ते हैं। सेनाएँ धूल से ढककर पहचानी नहीं जातीं।","te":"సాత్యకి ధృష్టద్యుమ్నుని రక్షిస్తాడు; అతని అద్భుత కార్యాన్ని చూసి ద్రోణుడు రణభూమిని చీకటి చేసే బాణాలతో అతనితో పోరాడతాడు. సేనలు దుమ్ముతో కప్పబడి గుర్తుపట్టలేరు.","ta":"சாத்யகி த்ருஷ்டத்யும்னனைக் காக்க, அவன் அற்புதச் செயலைக் கண்ட த்ரோணர் களத்தை இருளாக்கும் அம்புகளால் அவனுடன் போரிடுகிறார். படைகள் புழுதியில் மூழ்கி அடையாளம் தெரியாமல் போகின்றன.","ml":"സാത്യകി ധൃഷ്ടദ്യുമ്നനെ രക്ഷിക്കുന്നു; ആ അത്ഭുതകൃത്യം കണ്ട ദ്രോണർ, രംഗം ഇരുട്ടാക്കുന്ന അമ്പുകളുമായി അദ്ദേഹത്തോട് പോരാടുന്നു. പൊടിയിൽ മൂടി ഇരുസേനകളും തിരിച്ചറിയാനാകാത്തവിധമാകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.73; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"जयद्रथवधपर्व","titleEn":"Jayadrathavadha Parva (Slaying of Jayadratha)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"बाणे तस्मिन्निकृत्ते तु धृष्टद्युम्ने च मोक्षिते ।\nतेन वृष्णिप्रवीरेण युयुधानेन संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya, when that arrow was cut down and Dhrishtadyumna was freed by Yuyudhana, that Vrishni hero,"}},{"n":2,"text":"अमर्षितो महेष्वासः सर्वशस्त्रभृतां वरः ।\nनरव्याघ्रः शिनेः पौत्रे द्रोणः किमकरोद्युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"what did Drona, the great archer, best of all weapon-bearers, tiger among men, enraged, do in the battle against the grandson of Shini?"}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"संप्रद्रुतः क्रोधविषो व्यादितास्यशरासनः ।\nतीक्ष्णधारेषुदशनः शितनाराचदंष्ट्रवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona rushed forward, his anger his poison, his bow a gaping mouth, sharp-edged arrows his fangs, keen iron arrows his teeth,"}},{"n":4,"text":"संरम्भामर्षताम्राक्षो महाहिरिव निःश्वसन् ।\nनरवीरप्रमुदितैः शोणैरश्वैर्महाजवैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"his eyes red with fury and wrath, hissing like a great serpent, with swift red horses delighted at the heroes of men,"}},{"n":5,"text":"उत्पतद्भिरिवाकाशं क्रमद्भिरिव सर्वतः ।\nरुक्मपुङ्खाञ्शरानस्यन्युयुधानमुपाद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"horses that seemed to leap into the sky and to stride in all directions, and shooting gold-feathered arrows he ran at Yuyudhana."}},{"n":6,"text":"शरपातमहावर्षं रथघोषबलाहकम् ।\nकार्मुकाकर्षविक्षिप्तं नाराचबहुविद्युतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was a cloud of Drona: arrow-falls its great rain, the rumble of the chariot its thunder, with iron arrows its many lightnings flung by the pull of the bow,"}},{"n":7,"text":"शक्तिखड्गाशनिधरं क्रोधवेगसमुत्थितम् ।\nद्रोणमेघमनावार्यं हयमारुतचोदितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"bearing spears, swords and thunderbolts, risen with the force of anger, irresistible, driven by the wind of his horses."}},{"n":8,"text":"दृष्ट्वैवाभिपतन्तं तं शूरः परपुरंजयः ।\nउवाच सूतं शैनेयः प्रहसन्युद्धदुर्मदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him bearing down, the brave Shaineya, conqueror of enemy cities, laughing, spoke to his charioteer, intoxicated with battle."}},{"n":9,"text":"एतं वै ब्राह्मणं क्रूरं स्वकर्मण्यनवस्थितम् ।\nआश्रयं धार्तराष्ट्रस्य राज्ञो दुःखभयावहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He said: This cruel brahmana, who has strayed from his own work, the support of King Dhritarashtra's son and the bringer of sorrow and fear, is the one to meet."}},{"n":10,"text":"शीघ्रं प्रजवितैरश्वैः प्रत्युद्याहि प्रहृष्टवत् ।\nआचार्यं राजपुत्राणां सततं शूरमानिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Go quickly with your horses at full speed, joyfully, against the teacher of princes, ever proud of being a hero."}},{"n":11,"text":"ततो रजतसंकाशा माधवस्य हयोत्तमाः ।\nद्रोणस्याभिमुखाः शीघ्रमगच्छन्वातरंहसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Madhava's best horses, silver-white and swift as wind, went quickly to face Drona."}},{"n":12,"text":"इषुजालावृतं घोरमन्धकारमनन्तरम् ।\nअनाधृष्यमिवान्येषां शूराणामभवत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"A dense, terrible darkness of nets of arrows, as if impenetrable to other warriors, arose there."}},{"n":13,"text":"ततः शीघ्रास्त्रविदुषोर्द्रोणसात्वतयोस्तदा ।\nनान्तरं शरवृष्टीनां दृश्यते नरसिंहयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, between Drona and the Satvata, both skilled in swift weapons, no gap could be seen in the rains of arrows, between those two man-lions."}},{"n":14,"text":"इषूणां संनिपातेन शब्दो धाराभिघातजः ।\nशुश्रुवे शक्रमुक्तानामशनीनामिव स्वनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"From the clash of arrows a noise was heard, born of the strike of the streams, like the sound of thunderbolts flung by Shakra."}},{"n":15,"text":"नाराचैरतिविद्धानां शराणां रूपमाबभौ ।\nआशीविषविदष्टानां सर्पाणामिव भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The arrows, deeply struck by iron arrows, looked like snakes bitten by venomous serpents, O Bharata."}},{"n":16,"text":"तयोर्ज्यातलनिर्घोषो व्यश्रूयत सुदारुणः ।\nअजस्रं शैलशृङ्गाणां वज्रेणाहन्यतामिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"A most terrible sound of their bowstring-guards was heard, as if mountain peaks were being struck without pause by the thunderbolt."}},{"n":17,"text":"उभयोस्तौ रथौ राजंस्ते चाश्वास्तौ च सारथी ।\nरुक्मपुङ्खैः शरैश्छन्नाश्चित्ररूपा बभुस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The chariots of both, O king, their horses, and both charioteers, covered with gold-feathered arrows, looked then of many shapes."}},{"n":18,"text":"निर्मलानामजिह्मानां नाराचानां विशां पते ।\nनिर्मुक्ताशीविषाभानां संपातोऽभूत्सुदारुणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The fall of the clean, straight iron arrows, shot like venomous snakes, O lord of men, was most terrible."}},{"n":19,"text":"उभयोः पतिते छत्रे तथैव पतितौ ध्वजौ ।\nउभौ रुधिरसिक्ताङ्गावुभौ च विजयैषिणौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"The umbrella of each fell, and likewise the banner of each; both had their limbs drenched with blood, and both sought victory."}},{"n":20,"text":"स्रवद्भिः शोणितं गात्रैः प्रस्रुताविव वारणौ ।\nअन्योन्यमभिविध्येतां जीवितान्तकरैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With bodies streaming blood like two elephants in rut, they pierced each other with life-ending arrows."}},{"n":21,"text":"गर्जितोत्क्रुष्टसंनादाः शङ्खदुन्दुभिनिस्वनाः ।\nउपारमन्महाराज व्याजहार न कश्चन ॥","meaning":{"en":"The roars, shouts, conch-sounds and drum-sounds stopped, great king; no one spoke."}},{"n":22,"text":"तूष्णींभूतान्यनीकानि योधा युद्धादुपारमन् ।\nददृशे द्वैरथं ताभ्यां जातकौतूहलो जनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The armies fell silent, and the warriors ceased fighting; the people watched their chariot-duel with rising wonder."}},{"n":23,"text":"रथिनो हस्तियन्तारो हयारोहाः पदातयः ।\nअवैक्षन्ताचलैर्नेत्रैः परिवार्य रथर्षभौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Chariot-warriors, elephant-drivers, horsemen and footmen stood around the two best of charioteers, watching with unmoving eyes."}},{"n":24,"text":"हस्त्यनीकान्यतिष्ठन्त तथानीकानि वाजिनाम् ।\nतथैव रथवाहिन्यः प्रतिव्यूह्य व्यवस्थिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The elephant divisions stood still, and the cavalry, and the chariot columns, drawn up in array."}},{"n":25,"text":"मुक्ताविद्रुमचित्रैश्च मणिकाञ्चनभूषितैः ।\nध्वजैराभरणैश्चित्रैः कवचैश्च हिरण्मयैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With banners, gold- and jewel-adorned and bright with pearls and coral, with many-coloured ornaments and golden armour,"}},{"n":26,"text":"वैजयन्तीपताकाभिः परिस्तोमाङ्गकम्बलैः ।\nविमलैर्निशितैः शस्त्रैर्हयानां च प्रकीर्णकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"with victory-flags and pennants, with saddle-cloths, coverlets and blankets, with clean sharp weapons and horse-whisks,"}},{"n":27,"text":"जातरूपमयीभिश्च राजतीभिश्च मूर्धसु ।\nगजानां कुम्भमालाभिर्दन्तवेष्टैश्च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"with gold and silver on the heads of elephants, with garlands on their temples and bindings on their tusks, O Bharata,"}},{"n":28,"text":"सबलाकाः सखद्योताः सैरावतशतह्रदाः ।\nअदृश्यन्तोष्णपर्याये मेघानामिव वागुराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"they were seen like the cloud-banks at the turn of the hot season, with cranes, fireflies, rainbows and lightning."}},{"n":29,"text":"अपश्यन्नस्मदीयाश्च ते च यौधिष्ठिराः स्थिताः ।\nतद्युद्धं युयुधानस्य द्रोणस्य च महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Our men, and those of Yudhishthira, stood and watched the fight between Yuyudhana and the great-souled Drona."}},{"n":30,"text":"विमानाग्रगता देवा ब्रह्मशक्रपुरोगमाः ।\nसिद्धचारणसंघाश्च विद्याधरमहोरगाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gods, led by Brahma and Shakra, stood at the front of their celestial cars, with hosts of siddhas and charanas, vidyadharas and great serpents."}},{"n":31,"text":"गतप्रत्यागताक्षेपैश्चित्रैः शस्त्रविघातिभिः ।\nविविधैर्विस्मयं जग्मुस्तयोः पुरुषसिंहयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They were amazed at the various strokes of those two man-lions, with advances and retreats, hurled and parried, many and strange."}},{"n":32,"text":"हस्तलाघवमस्त्रेषु दर्शयन्तौ महाबलौ ।\nअन्योन्यं समविध्येतां शरैस्तौ द्रोणसात्यकी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Displaying their lightness of hand in weapons, the two mighty men, Drona and Satyaki, pierced each other with arrows."}},{"n":33,"text":"ततो द्रोणस्य दाशार्हः शरांश्चिच्छेद संयुगे ।\nपत्रिभिः सुदृढैराशु धनुश्चैव महाद्युते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Satyaki, the Dasharha, quickly cut Drona's arrows in the battle with firm feathered arrows, and his bow too, O radiant king."}},{"n":34,"text":"निमेषान्तरमात्रेण भारद्वाजोऽपरं धनुः ।\nसज्यं चकार तच्चाशु चिच्छेदास्य स सात्यकिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the space of a blink Bharadvaja's son strung another bow, and Satyaki quickly cut that too."}},{"n":35,"text":"ततस्त्वरन्पुनर्द्रोणो धनुर्हस्तो व्यतिष्ठत ।\nसज्यं सज्यं पुनश्चास्य चिच्छेद निशितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Again Drona, in haste, stood with bow in hand, and again Satyaki cut each strung bow with sharp arrows."}},{"n":36,"text":"ततोऽस्य संयुगे द्रोणो दृष्ट्वा कर्मातिमानुषम् ।\nयुयुधानस्य राजेन्द्र मनसेदमचिन्तयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, seeing Yuyudhana's superhuman feat in the battle, Drona, O lord of kings, thought to himself:"}},{"n":37,"text":"एतदस्त्रबलं रामे कार्तवीर्ये धनंजये ।\nभीष्मे च पुरुषव्याघ्रे यदिदं सात्वतां वरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"This strength in weapons is in Rama, in Kartavirya, in Dhananjaya, in Bhishma, tiger among men, and in this best of the Satvatas."}},{"n":38,"text":"तं चास्य मनसा द्रोणः पूजयामास विक्रमम् ।\nलाघवं वासवस्येव संप्रेक्ष्य द्विजसत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In his mind Drona honoured his valour, seeing a nimbleness like Indra's, that best of brahmanas."}},{"n":39,"text":"तुतोषास्त्रविदां श्रेष्ठस्तथा देवाः सवासवाः ।\nन तामालक्षयामासुर्लघुतां शीघ्रकारिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The best of those who know weapons was pleased, as were the gods with Indra; they could not even see the swift mover's speed."}},{"n":40,"text":"देवाश्च युयुधानस्य गन्धर्वाश्च विशां पते ।\nसिद्धचारणसंघाश्च विदुर्द्रोणस्य कर्म तत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The gods, the gandharvas, and the hosts of siddhas and charanas, O lord of men, recognised that deed of Drona as well as Yuyudhana's."}},{"n":41,"text":"ततोऽन्यद्धनुरादाय द्रोणः क्षत्रियमर्दनः ।\nअस्त्रैरस्त्रविदां श्रेष्ठो योधयामास भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Drona, crusher of kshatriyas, took another bow and fought, the best of those who know weapons, with weapons, O Bharata."}},{"n":42,"text":"तस्यास्त्राण्यस्त्रमायाभिः प्रतिहन्य स सात्यकिः ।\nजघान निशितैर्बाणैस्तदद्भुतमिवाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Satyaki, turning back his weapons with the magic of weapons, struck him with sharp arrows; it seemed a marvel."}},{"n":43,"text":"तस्यातिमानुषं कर्म दृष्ट्वान्यैरसमं रणे ।\nयुक्तं योगेन योगज्ञास्तावकाः समपूजयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that superhuman deed, which none other in battle could equal, joined to yoga, those of yours who knew yoga honoured him."}},{"n":44,"text":"यदस्त्रमस्यति द्रोणस्तदेवास्यति सात्यकिः ।\nतमाचार्योऽप्यसंभ्रान्तोऽयोधयच्छत्रुतापनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever weapon Drona shot, Satyaki shot the same, and the teacher, scorcher of foes, fought him unflustered."}},{"n":45,"text":"ततः क्रुद्धो महाराज धनुर्वेदस्य पारगः ।\nवधाय युयुधानस्य दिव्यमस्त्रमुदैरयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, in anger, O great king, Drona, master of the science of the bow, sent up a divine weapon to kill Yuyudhana."}},{"n":46,"text":"तदाग्नेयं महाघोरं रिपुघ्नमुपलक्ष्य सः ।\nअस्त्रं दिव्यं महेष्वासो वारुणं समुदैरयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that very terrible fire-weapon, slayer of foes, Satyaki, the great archer, sent up the divine Varuna weapon."}},{"n":47,"text":"हाहाकारो महानासीद्दृष्ट्वा दिव्यास्त्रधारिणौ ।\nन विचेरुस्तदाकाशे भूतान्याकाशगान्यपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"A great cry of woe went up, seeing the two wielding divine weapons; even creatures moving in the sky did not move in the sky then."}},{"n":48,"text":"अस्त्रे ते वारुणाग्नेये ताभ्यां बाणसमाहिते ।\nन तावदभिषज्येते व्यावर्तदथ भास्करः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Varuna and Agneya weapons, fixed on the arrows by the two, did not yet collide, when the sun began to turn."}},{"n":49,"text":"ततो युधिष्ठिरो राजा भीमसेनश्च पाण्डवः ।\nनकुलः सहदेवश्च पर्यरक्षन्त सात्यकिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Yudhishthira, Bhimasena the Pandava, Nakula and Sahadeva protected Satyaki."}},{"n":50,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नमुखैः सार्धं विराटश्च सकेकयः ।\nमत्स्याः शाल्वेयसेनाश्च द्रोणमाजग्मुरञ्जसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Virata with the Kekayas, the Matsyas and the Shalveya troops, with Dhrishtadyumna and others in front, came swiftly against Drona."}},{"n":51,"text":"दुःशासनं पुरस्कृत्य राजपुत्राः सहस्रशः ।\nद्रोणमभ्युपपद्यन्त सपत्नैः परिवारितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With Duhshasana in front, thousands of princes came to Drona, who was surrounded by his enemies."}},{"n":52,"text":"ततो युद्धमभूद्राजंस्तव तेषां च धन्विनाम् ।\nरजसा संवृते लोके शरजालसमावृते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a battle arose, O king, between your archers and theirs, the world covered with dust and with nets of arrows."}},{"n":53,"text":"सर्वमाविग्नमभवन्न प्राज्ञायत किंचन ।\nसैन्येन रजसा ध्वस्ते निर्मर्यादमवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"All was in turmoil; nothing could be distinguished. With the army and the dust everything was confounded, and there was no order."}}]}]}